---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy — POYARA" description="How the POYARA studio website handles visitor information, hosting data and external links.">
  <section class="page-header wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">SITE INFORMATION / 01</p>
    <h1>Privacy, <em>plainly.</em></h1>
    <p>What this website does—and does not—do with visitor information.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="section wrap case-grid">
    <div class="case-main policy-copy">
      <p class="policy-updated">Last updated: October 21, 2026</p>
      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <p>This is a static, informational website. POYARA does not currently provide an account, enquiry form or newsletter sign-up here. The site does not intentionally collect names, email addresses or messages from visitors.</p>
      <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p>POYARA has not installed an advertising pixel, analytics service or tracking-cookie feature on these pages. The site's small JavaScript enhancements are for navigation, scrolling and visual interaction; they do not store a visitor profile.</p>
      <h2>Hosting and technical data</h2>
      <p>If the website is served through GitHub Pages, GitHub handles the delivery infrastructure. According to GitHub's documentation, GitHub Pages logs visitors' IP addresses for security purposes, including for visitors who are not signed in. This processing is outside POYARA's direct control. See <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/what-is-github-pages" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Pages documentation</a> and the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Privacy Statement</a>.</p>
      <h2>Portfolio media from Adobe and Behance</h2>
      <p>The homepage loads preview images for selected public portfolio projects from Behance's image delivery network. These image requests may disclose technical connection data, such as an IP address, to the media provider. If you choose to play a portfolio film, an Adobe Creative Cloud video player is loaded in an embedded frame. Adobe may then process connection information according to its own privacy practices. The video player is not requested until you press play. See <a href="https://www.adobe.com/privacy/policy.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Adobe's Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
      <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
      <p>Links to project demonstrations, source repositories and third-party resources open websites with their own privacy practices. Their operators may process information when you visit them.</p>
      <h2>Changes and questions</h2>
      <p>This notice describes the current website, not future services or products. It will be revised if features or hosting arrangements change. For privacy questions, contact Mohammad Mohammadzadeh at <a href="mailto:Lightnermax@gmail.com">Lightnermax@gmail.com</a>, or see the <a href={withBase('contact/')}>contact page</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <aside class="case-meta">
      <p class="eyebrow">AT A GLANCE</p>
      <div><span>Site format</span><strong>Static public pages</strong></div>
      <div><span>Site analytics</span><strong>Not installed</strong></div>
      <div><span>Visitor accounts</span><strong>Not provided</strong></div>
      <div><span>Hosting</span><strong>GitHub Pages</strong></div>
      <a class="text-link" href={withBase('site-information/')}>Other site information ↗</a>
    </aside>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
